{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems","id":597840,"title":"Can animals take Totems?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-20T21:36:18-07:00","id":597840,"title":"Can animals take Totems?","content":"If an animal were to become sapient, could it appeal to a Totem for Patronage? It's a cheat, but I am ultimately asking if a boar or head of cattle with a thread of extinct shifter blood in them could have it's mind enhanced with magic and appeal to Suzuka to strengthen the shifter blood in them, allowing them to give birth to a superior bloodline who in turn can do the same.<br /> <br /> Edit: Alternaitvely, what do you think might happen if you took one of the weak kinfolk to The Coil in the Flux?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-21-2015, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T23:06:52-07:00","id":597935,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really seem to be supported in the text. Totems don't just bond with anything with shifter blood<br /> <br /> If you wanted to have a special animal that's been blessed like that, you can always make a Gorgon or a Kami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T00:28:32-07:00","id":598020,"title":"","content":"Well, they DO bond with Shamans. And not just Awakened Shamans, either. They also take on Sorcerer shamans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T01:06:53-07:00","id":598044,"title":"","content":"Ok. So yes. If somehow an animal managed to become a sorcerer shaman, it could theoretically obtain the Totem background.<br /> <br /> But that's a fairly gigantic stretch of the text.<br /> <br /> Is there a reason why something like a Gorgon or Kami wouldn't suit your needs mechanically? It certainly seems to fill the narrative role of &quot;sentient animal is spiritual backing&quot; just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T02:50:00-07:00","id":598089,"title":"","content":"Follow up question, if a toaster gained sentience and became a shaman could it take a totem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T04:30:38-07:00","id":598150,"title":"","content":"Note that the whole totem-gaining business in Werewolf is tied to The Pact, the accord that the spirits have with the Garou tribes (or was it the Garou Nation?). Anyone else will have a far more difficult time with that since the spirits are not bound to concepts like chiminage in regard to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T06:40:18-07:00","id":598266,"title":"","content":"What you are purposing is far fetched but its neither supported by nor discouraged by the existing text. The Skullpigs are supposedly the last descendants of the Grondr and by eating the remains of wyrm creatures they have the ability to become intelligent and over time manifest powers (some editions say sorcerer like magic, i think 20th says gifts, can't remember off the top of my head). They however never talk about them making pacts with spirits. Animal Kami on the other hand can make pacts with totem spirits but they have a more profound awareness of the spirit world and are already being groomed by Gaia or one of pantheon.<br /> <br /> A head of cattle could never become shifters because they have been domesticated, this is the same rationale for why domesticated dogs can't mate true with Garou. The Grondr are up the creek because as mentioned above, after their fall their animal kin fell as well. Best scenario for rebirth is that some of the old breed returning from Umbra, making an alliance with the mokole to get access to their gift that allows them to choose new breeding partners, choosing a wild bovine/bison and boar/warthog to restart their lines with but that is just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:16:09-07:00","id":598430,"title":"","content":"Dwight is right, if two stupendously unlikely things happen to a thing that could not normally take a totem, than yeah, that thing could take a totem.<br /> <br /> I don't even see the point though. What narrative purpose does it serve?<br /> <br /> In this game there are lots of things that turn into animals, spirit-possessed animals, and actual spirits of animals. Making a flesh and blood animal capable of conscious thought so it can then have supernatural powers seems kinda silly and redundant. If you want a hyper intelligent spiritually aware wolf character, there are plenty of ways to get that exact thing without the plot contortions necessary to justify an individual genius Canis Lupus with connections to the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T10:16:09-07:00","id":598481,"title":"","content":"I am just brain storming here, as I am currently thinking about a game revolving around my homebrew &quot;Fellowship of Ma'at&quot; which revolves around an alliance between Striders, Mokole, Mummies, and the human Children of Osiris as well as a sprinkling of Dreamspeakers. I never got to run the campaign, and I am looking for ideas on what they could be doing together with their joint resources. Besides wailing on the Setites.<br /> <br /> Edit: In The Red Sign, the Traditions, Technocracy, and assorted vampires all changed the world. I am trying to recreate a bit of that in the Fellowship of Ma'at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-21-2015, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:56:17-07:00","id":598634,"title":"","content":"Follow up question for my brave little toaster, I'm going to have it communicate through pictograms burned into bread but for the life of me I can't think of a totem for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T00:56:24-07:00","id":599075,"title":"","content":"What kind of changing the world is involved in giving totems to animals? What purpose does it serve? Do the animals actually want to serve and emulate something that's not within their own perception of life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T01:22:51-07:00","id":599083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems?p=598634#post598634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow up question for my brave little toaster, I'm going to have it communicate through pictograms burned into bread but for the life of me I can't think of a totem for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Totem is the Rosetta Stone. It's not actually THE spirit of the Rosetta Stone, but that is the form it takes now, when manifesting before supplicants. It was originally a spirit that dwelled within cave paintings, but it grew as written language became more common. Now it is the Totem of all written forms of communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T01:25:36-07:00","id":599085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems?p=599075#post599075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of changing the world is involved in giving totems to animals? What purpose does it serve? Do the animals actually want to serve and emulate something that's not within their own perception of life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Suzuka is the Totem of royal bloodlines and her children gain an automatic extra dot in their Breeding Background. The animals I am talking about are the weak blooded kinfolk of extinct shapeshifters that could change the world if they are brought back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T03:17:25-07:00","id":599148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems?p=599083#post599083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Totem is the Rosetta Stone. It's not actually THE spirit of the Rosetta Stone, but that is the form it takes now, when manifesting before supplicants. It was originally a spirit that dwelled within cave paintings, but it grew as written language became more common. Now it is the Totem of all written forms of communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>A totem by definition is I quote &quot;a natural object or animal believed by a particular society to have spiritual significance and adopted by it as an emblem.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not buying it, the totem of all written forms of communication. Lets call it the totem of the #Hashtag. You can't just assign totem status to an abstract thought or thing. A people or society have to assign a spiritual significance to it, noir can you say something as basic as communication has a spiritual representation in the spirit world. <br /> <br /> Toasty as I now call him will be the small chrome variable browning setting shaman of Wheat, after all wheat is a natural object which has spiritual significance to a particular society.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:46:18-07:00","id":599463,"title":"","content":"You could always go with Clashing Boom Boom or Grandfather Thunder for those times people are stupid enough to stick a knife in you to get the toast out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:50:34-07:00","id":599479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems?p=599085#post599085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The animals I am talking about are the weak blooded kinfolk of extinct shapeshifters that could change the world if they are brought back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. This seems an incredibly &quot;meh&quot; way of handling it. Bringing the extinct Fera back should be a much bigger deal than a spirit going, &quot;you know what? We need some Apis back, lets go magic up some cows.&quot;<br /> <br /> And even then, this doesn't explain why the Kami route isn't more preferable. Kami can have the Shapeshifter Kin power, which gives them Pure Breed 3 to a single Changing Breed for one purchase (they can actually get multiple affinities and even be universal kin to all Gaian aligned shifters). It's a power that works even with splats that don't normally get Pure Breed (so you can have a Kami with Pure Breed 3 for Bone Gnawers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems?p=599148#post599148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not buying it, the totem of all written forms of communication. Lets call it the totem of the #Hashtag. You can't just assign totem status to an abstract thought or thing. A people or society have to assign a spiritual significance to it, noir can you say something as basic as communication has a spiritual representation in the spirit world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm, I think you're getting a bit too harsh here. The setting of WtA definitely allows this. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:24:20-07:00","id":599736,"title":"","content":"There is a prophecy is that Gaia can win it all of her different children work together. It seems to me that bringing back an extinct Fera would be on par with a Perfect Metis chronicle. And Kami can't breed true to create more of their kind. Besides, think of all the story seeds involved. Whoever gets the privilege of raising the newborn Fera will have a major propaganda tool as to who should lead the Garou Nation and possibly the Ahldi. If a Shadow Lord, Uktena, Glass Walker, or Black Fury gets their hands on the kid, and that kid can drastically raise the odds of Breeding true and make more like himself, the Garou Nation, even the Uktena and Wendigo, will have to start listening to that Tribe about the direction of the Garou Nation and the need for new leadership. It won't guarantee that they get to be the new rulers, but it's a great place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:20:14-07:00","id":599949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems?p=599736#post599736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Kami can't breed true to create more of their kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>... why not? I mean, Kami can't breed more Kami, but if a Kami is made out of a kin animal, there's nothing that says that goes away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whoever gets the privilege of raising the newborn Fera will have a major propaganda tool as to who should lead the Garou Nation and possibly the Ahldi. </div> </div> </div>I think you're overstating this a bit.<br /> <br /> A pack that manages something, even something this big, isn't going to get a whole Tribe's reputation to skyrocket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T21:47:22-07:00","id":600172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/597840-can-animals-take-totems?p=598089#post598089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow up question, if a toaster gained sentience and became a shaman could it take a totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, is the toaster plugged in or not?!?<br /> <br /> How do you expect an answer without us knowing this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","v